Exit code 1

- The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).

## Measured semantics — out of scope

These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` record the measured semantics that hook features specify against. The `onError` boundary remains out of scope; issue #93 defines the aggregate usage delivered after tool rounds.

- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the summed provider-call usage for the entire turn, so tool rounds are included in a deployer's billing or audit total ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
- A provider round that reports no usage adds nothing to the turn's total, and a turn in which no round reported usage passes `undefined` to `afterModelResponse` rather than zero or `NaN` ([validated by: counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
- The turn total adds each token field of every reporting round to the running total ([validated by: adds each token field of a round to the running total](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L31)); a round that reports nothing keeps the total unchanged ([validated by: keeps the total when a round reports nothing](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L36)), the first reporting round starts the total ([validated by: starts from the round when there is no total](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40)), and with no reporting round there is no total ([validated by: reports nothing when no round reported](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L44)).
import {shouldContinueToolLoop, sumUsage} from './orchestratorHelpers.js';
import type {ToolRegistry} from './tools/registry.js';
import type {ToolCall} from '../types/ai.js';

// All three conditions matter; dropping the registry check spins the tool loop.

const A_TOOL: ToolCall[] = [{id: 't1', name: 'lookup', input: {}}];
const REGISTRY = {} as ToolRegistry;

describe('shouldContinueToolLoop', () => {
  it('continues when the model requested a tool and a registry can run it', () => {
    expect(shouldContinueToolLoop('tool_use', A_TOOL, REGISTRY)).toBe(true);
  });

  it('stops when no registry is configured, whatever the model asked for', () => {
    expect(shouldContinueToolLoop('tool_use', A_TOOL, undefined)).toBe(false);
  });

  it('stops when the model named no tool', () => {
    expect(shouldContinueToolLoop('tool_use', [], REGISTRY)).toBe(false);
  });

  it('stops when the model finished for a reason other than tool use', () => {
    expect(shouldContinueToolLoop('end_turn', A_TOOL, REGISTRY)).toBe(false);
  });
});

describe('sumUsage', () => {
  const usage = {inputTokens: 1, outputTokens: 2, totalTokens: 3};

  it('adds each token field of a round to the running total', () => {
    const total = sumUsage(usage, {inputTokens: 10, outputTokens: 20, totalTokens: 30});
    expect(total).toEqual({inputTokens: 11, outputTokens: 22, totalTokens: 33});
  });

  it('keeps the total when a round reports nothing', () => {
    expect(sumUsage(usage, undefined)).toEqual(usage);
  });

  it('starts from the round when there is no total', () => {
    expect(sumUsage(undefined, usage)).toEqual(usage);
  });

  it('reports nothing when no round reported', () => {
    expect(sumUsage(undefined, undefined)).toBeUndefined();
  });
});
